    "body": "# Brown — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Brown University\n\nDegree route: ScM in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nBrown CS ScM: 8 graded graduate courses within ~2 years (or ~1.5–16 months accelerated). Comprehensive or AI/ML tracks; optional professional internships and CSCI 2980 research project.\n\nOrientation: 8 courses · Comprehensive or AI/ML · ~1.5–2 years\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$43,908 — Academic-year tuition (ScM Computer Science, 4 courses × per-course rate); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nBrown Student Financial Services / Graduate Funding COA 2026–27: Computer Science master’s per-course rate $10,977. Standard track for ScM CS is 8 courses; COA budgets 2 courses/term → AY tuition $21,954 × 2 = $43,908. Estimated total program tuition at the published rate = $87,816. Mandatory fees in the COA (~$1,596 AY at the 2+2 pattern) and health insurance are separate. Program may also be completed as 8 courses in one year.\n\nApplication timing: Fall: 15 Jan (month-day; year not labeled) · Spring: 1 Nov · Fifth-year Fall: 1 May. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS overview](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://sfs.brown.edu/tuition-and-fees/graduate)\n- [COA by program (CS)](https://gradfunding.brown.edu/cost-attendance-program)\n- [Graduate Programs ScM Computer Science (deadlines)](https://graduateprograms.brown.edu/graduate-program/computer-science-scm)\n- [Brown CS Applying to Master's](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/applications/)\n- [SPS Deadlines and Credits (CS Fall Jan. 15)](https://masters.brown.edu/admissions/tuition-aid/deadlines-credits)\n- [Comprehensive track requirements](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/reqs/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
