    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/cornell-cs.md",
    "title": "Cornell — MS / MEng",
    "body": "# Cornell — MS / MEng\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#7 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Cornell University\n\nDegree route: MS / MEng in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nResearch MS is a selective four-semester (≈2-year) degree: 34 credits with 6–12 thesis credits, an outside minor, and a written thesis + oral. Professional MEng is a separate ~1-year coursework + capstone route.\n\nOrientation: MS research thesis · or MEng professional · Distinct routes\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$29,500 — Academic-year tuition (Endowed research master’s MS); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nBursar: Endowed Research Master’s (M.S. and listed M.A./non-degree) $14,750/semester, $29,500/year (2026–27). CS MS admitted students receive full tuition, stipend, and health insurance via required TA-ships each of four semesters—so billed tuition is typically covered for admitted students. Separately, M.Eng is Professional Tier 1: $36,973/semester, $73,946/year (self-supported).\n\nApplication timing: MS: 18 Jan for Fall (month-day as posted; year/timezone not labeled) · MEng Fall: 1 Feb; MEng Spring: 1 Oct. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram pages emphasize distinct MS vs M.Eng routes; funding policies differ — do not assume PhD funding for either. Specific M.Eng/MS CS assistantship guarantees not verified on bursar page.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CS MS apply](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/master-science-computer-science/apply)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://bursar.cornell.edu/students-parents/tuition-rates-and-fees)\n- [MEng apply](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/master-engineering-computer-science/apply)\n- [Master of Science in Computer Science](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/master-science-computer-science)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
