    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/harvard-cs.md",
    "title": "Harvard — Related SM",
    "body": "# Harvard — Related SM\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#19 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Harvard University\n\nDegree route: Related master’s: Computational Science and Engineering\n\nApplication status: Related CSE degree · not standalone CS\n\n## Academic direction\n\nHarvard SEAS has no open terminal CS master's for external applicants. CS SM is for current Harvard PhD/A.B. students; related terminal master's are CSE and Data Science.\n\nOrientation: Restricted · No external terminal CS SM\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$67,504 — Program / full-year tuition (SEAS CSE SM) — related alternative, not a pure CS MS; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Availability: Computational Science and Engineering SM (related SEAS master’s), not a standalone CS MS.\n\nHarvard Griffin GSAS Cost of Attendance 2026–27: SEAS Computational Science and Engineering master of science (SM) full-year cost $67,504 (one-year program). CSE ME and Data Science SM use $67,504 first year / $33,752 subsequent listed terms. Per-course rates if less than full-time: $8,438 / $16,876 / $25,314 / $33,752 for 1–4 courses per term. Standard GSAS full tuition for other master’s/PhD years 1–2 is $59,048—not used here. Catalog harvard-cs uses this CSE-related SM figure with an alternative-route label; Harvard does not publish a separate terminal MS Computer Science under this id.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open (Fall 2027 CSE/Data Science portal open) · Deadline 1 Dec 2026 · 5:00 p.m. ET (CSE SM). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CSE master's](https://seas.harvard.edu/masters-computational-science-and-engineering)\n- [Official tuition / budget (GSAS COA)](https://gsas.harvard.edu/apply/cost-attendance-2026-2027)\n- [SEAS CSE How to Apply (Fall 2027; Dec 1, 2026)](https://seas.harvard.edu/masters-computational-science-and-engineering/how-apply)\n- [GSAS Computational Science and Engineering (SM/ME Dec 01, 2026 05:00 pm)](https://gsas.harvard.edu/program/computational-science-and-engineering)\n- [CS graduate program (PhD focus)](https://seas.harvard.edu/computer-science/graduate-program)\n- [SM and ME course requirements](https://seas.harvard.edu/office-academic-programs/graduate-policies-procedures-and-forms/sm-and-me-degrees/sm-and-me-area)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
