    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/illinois-cs.md",
    "title": "Illinois Urbana-Champaign — MS / MCS",
    "body": "# Illinois Urbana-Champaign — MS / MCS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#5 in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n\nDegree route: MS / Master of Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nSiebel School offers a 32-credit professional MCS (coursework-only; Urbana typically ≤3 consecutive semesters) and a separate 32-credit research MS (thesis via CS 599). Eight optional graduate tracks (AI, data science, security, etc.).\n\nOrientation: MCS or research MS · 32 credits · 8 tracks\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$40,444 — Academic-year tuition (MCS / Engineering, international or nonresident, Range I 12+ hours); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nRegistrar: Engineering and Engineering Related Programs (including Computer Science) — Nonresident or International Range I (12+ hours) $20,222/semester ($40,444 AY Fall+Spring). Resident Range I $10,636/semester ($21,272 AY). Range II (6–11 hours) nonresident/international $13,482/semester ($26,964 AY); Illinois Cost Calculator for MCS international at 9 credits matches Range II. Campus fees and living costs are extra. Online MCS uses a different per-credit schedule—not recorded here.\n\nApplication timing: MCS Urbana Fall: 1 May · 11:59 p.m. CT (annual month-day; year not labeled) · MS thesis Fall: 1 Dec · 11:59 p.m. CT. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMCS: eligible to accept RA/TA if offered; opportunities limited and not guaranteed (Siebel MCS tuition page). Do not apply PhD funding policies to MCS/MS.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Graduate FAQs](https://siebelschool.illinois.edu/admissions/graduate/faqs)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.registrar.illinois.edu/g-tuition-rates-2627/)\n- [Credit-hour ranges](https://www.registrar.illinois.edu/g-tuition-cr-2627/)\n- [MCS tuition page](https://siebelschool.illinois.edu/academics/graduate/professional-mcs/tuition-fees)\n- [Cost calculator MCS international 9 cr](https://cost.illinois.edu/Home/Cost/I/G/10KS0112MCS/9/120268/120268)\n- [Application deadlines](https://siebelschool.illinois.edu/admissions/graduate/application-deadlines)\n- [MCS program](https://siebelschool.illinois.edu/academics/graduate/professional-mcs)\n- [Computer Science, MCS catalog 2026–27](https://catalog.illinois.edu/graduate/engineering/computer-science-mcs/)\n- [Computer Science, MS catalog 2026–27](https://catalog.illinois.edu/graduate/engineering/computer-science-ms/)\n- [M.S. Program](https://siebelschool.illinois.edu/academics/graduate/ms-program)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
