    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/jhu-cs.md",
    "title": "Johns Hopkins — MSE",
    "body": "# Johns Hopkins — MSE\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#21 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Johns Hopkins University\n\nDegree route: MSE in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nJHU CS MSE: 10 courses or 8 + research; ~3 semesters typical. Breadth across ≥4 of 5 areas; optional AI track and HLT concentration.\n\nOrientation: 8+research or 10 courses · ~3 semesters · AI/HLT options\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$68,670 — Academic-year tuition (WSE residential master’s / PhD full-time); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nJohns Hopkins Whiting School of Engineering Cost of Attendance: WSE Residential Master’s and PhD Full-time Tuition $68,670 annually / $34,335 per semester (2026–27). The separately listed “Non-resident Fee” $6,868 annually is a part-time/non-resident enrollment status charge, not an out-of-state surcharge for on-campus full-time students—do not add it to the residential full-time figure. Matriculation fee $500 and living/insurance costs are separate. MSE CS is the full-time residential route.\n\nApplication timing: Fall: 15 Feb · 11:59 p.m. EST · Spring: 1 Oct · 11:59 p.m. EST (month-day; year not labeled). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MSE CS program (brochure landing)](https://www.cs.jhu.edu/mse-programs-original/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://engineering.jhu.edu/education/graduate-studies/graduate-financial-aid/affording-your-education/)\n- [MSE CS program](https://www.cs.jhu.edu/academic-programs/graduate-studies/masters-computer-science/)\n- [MSE CS Admissions (deadlines)](https://www.cs.jhu.edu/academic-programs/graduate-studies/masters-computer-science/admissions/)\n- [MSE CS program](https://www.cs.jhu.edu/academic-programs/graduate-studies/mse-programs/)\n- [Catalogue MSE CS](https://e-catalogue.jhu.edu/engineering/full-time-residential-programs/degree-programs/computer-science/computer-science-master-science-engineering/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
