    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/maryland-cs.md",
    "title": "Maryland — MS",
    "body": "# Maryland — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#12 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Maryland, College Park\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: CSMS route · confirm catalog distinction\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUMD CS MS is 30 credits with thesis (6 CMSC 799) or non-thesis scholarly paper. Four qualifying courses across four of eight areas; complete within five years.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · Thesis or scholarly paper · 8 areas\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$34,488 — Academic-year tuition (graduate nonresident, 9 credits × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUMD Student Financial Services Fall 2026 & Spring 2027: graduate Non-Resident tuition $1,916/credit (Resident $913). Academic-year reference at 9 credits/semester (mandatory campus-fee plateau) = $17,244 × 2 = $34,488. Campus fees for 9+ credits: $738/semester ($1,476 AY) not included in the tuition figure. Extended Studies CS professional page lists the same out-of-state per-credit rate and estimates 30-credit total master’s tuition $57,480 (out-of-state). SHIP (~$2,939 AY) and international student fee $125/semester are separate. MS is 30 credits.\n\nApplication timing: 4 Dec 2026 · MS application page. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nCS apply page; financial aid specifics for MS not fully verified. Do not assume PhD funding.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Grad apply](https://www.cs.umd.edu/grad/apply)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://billpay.umd.edu/GraduateTuition)\n- [Extended Studies CS tuition](https://exst.umd.edu/professionals-post-baccalaureates/professional-graduate-programs/computer-science/tuition-and-fees)\n- [MS prospective / catalog](https://www.cs.umd.edu/grad/ms-catalog)\n- [CMSC catalog — different MS route](https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/graduate/programs/computer-science-cmsc/computer-science-ms/)\n- [Rank 12 cross-check · May 2026](https://science.umd.edu/newsletters/cs/2026-05.html)\n- [M.S. degree requirements](https://www.cs.umd.edu/grad/ms-policy-manual)\n- [Catalog CSMS](https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/graduate/programs/computer-science-csms/computer-science-ms/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
