    "title": "Michigan — MS",
    "body": "# Michigan — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Michigan, Ann Arbor\n\nDegree route: MS / MSE in Computer Science and Engineering\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nCSE master’s requires 30 credits; thesis optional; normally finished in 1.5–2 years. MS vs MSE is primarily naming/eligibility by prior engineering bachelor’s.\n\nOrientation: 30 credits · Optional thesis · 1.5–2 years\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$68,038 — Academic-year tuition (College of Engineering graduate, nonresident full-time × 2 full terms); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nRegistrar College of Engineering Graduate Full Term 2026–27: Michigan Non-Resident 9+ (Full-Time) $34,019 per full term; Michigan Resident $18,308. Typical academic year = Fall + Winter full terms → nonresident $68,038. CSE MS/MSE uses Engineering graduate rates. Master’s funding is not guaranteed at admission.\n\nApplication timing: Apps reopen mid-Sep (Rackham; late Aug/early Sep noted) · Master's deadline 15 Jan · 11:59 p.m. ET (FA 2027 cycle referenced on page). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nCSE master’s pages historically note limited funding; do not assume PhD support. Specific 2026–27 MS funding guarantees not verified on tuition page.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Master’s in CSE](https://cse.engin.umich.edu/academics/graduate/graduate-programs/masters-in-cse/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://ro.umich.edu/tuition-residency/tuition-fees/2026-2027/graduate/full-term/college-engineering-graduate-full-term)\n- [CSE graduate admissions](https://cse.engin.umich.edu/academics/graduate/admissions/)\n- [CSE how to apply](https://cse.engin.umich.edu/academics/graduate/admissions/apply/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
