    "title": "Princeton — MSE / MEng",
    "body": "# Princeton — MSE / MEng\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#6 in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Princeton University\n\nDegree route: MSE / MEng in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Fall 2027 master’s intake suspended\n\n## Academic direction\n\nPrinceton CS master's (MSE/M.Eng.): normally 2 years with 6 courses + thesis (MSE) or non-thesis M.Eng. Department is not accepting master's applications for Fall 2027 admission.\n\nOrientation: Restricted F27 · No apps · Curriculum 2yr when open\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$65,210 — Academic-year tuition (Graduate School regular rate) — applications suspended Fall 2027; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 sticker reference only. Availability: CS will not accept master’s applications for Fall 2027.\n\nPrinceton CS department: will not accept applications to the master’s degree program for Fall 2027 admission (resource uncertainty); MSE/M.Eng. are normally fully funded via teaching assistantships when offered. Graduate School University Rates 2026–27: Tuition Regular Rate $65,210; SHP Fee $4,220 (total $69,430)—SHP not included in the tuition figure. Rate recorded as published sticker with clear closed/suspended availability for Fall 2027 entry; not a billable quote for new Fall 2027 master’s admits.\n\nApplication timing: No Fall 2027 MS deadline — CS will not accept master's applications for Fall 2027 (MSE closed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nThe department describes funded master’s degrees, but has suspended Fall 2027 admission. This is not an available Fall 2027 funding opportunity.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Master's degree (no F27 apps)](https://www.cs.princeton.edu/grad/masters-degree-requirements)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Grad School rates)](https://gradschool.princeton.edu/financial-support/financial-support-model/funding-calendar-university-rates-costs)\n- [Grad School Application Deadlines (no M.S.E. admission Fall 2027 for CS)](https://gradschool.princeton.edu/admission-onboarding/prepare/application-deadlines)\n- [MSE track](https://www.cs.princeton.edu/grad/mse-track)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
