    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/purdue-cs.md",
    "title": "Purdue — MS",
    "body": "# Purdue — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Purdue University, West Lafayette\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nPurdue CS MS: typically 3–4 semesters. Non-thesis 10 courses or thesis 8 courses + CS 69800. Required cores in Systems I/II and Algorithms plus breadth across areas.\n\nOrientation: 10 courses or thesis · Systems + algorithms cores · 3–4 semesters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$29,918 — Academic-year tuition and mandatory fees (CS & Engineering graduate, nonresident, 8+ hours × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nPurdue Bursar Graduate Tuition and Fees 2026–27: Computer Science & Engineering flat rate (8+ credit hours) Non-Resident sub-total tuition $14,959/semester → $29,918 AY (includes General Service, Fitness/Wellness, Student Activity, Nonresident Tuition, and Differential General Service $562/semester). Indiana Resident CS&E sub-total $5,558/semester ($11,116 AY). International students add International Fee $200/semester ($400 AY) on top of the nonresident CS&E total ($15,159/semester; $30,318 AY). Separately, Professional Master’s “MA in Computer Science” is billed per credit ($1,413.25 nonresident/international; 30-credit estimate $42,397.50)—not used here; the catalog master’s curriculum page is the standard on-campus MS. Living costs extra.\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 start — 1 Dec 2026 · Spring 2027 start — 1 Oct 2026 (MS and PhD; West Lafayette). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Master's program curriculum](https://www.cs.purdue.edu/graduate/curriculum/masters.html)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.purdue.edu/treasurer/finance/bursar-office/tuition/fee-rates-2026-2027/graduate-tuition-and-fees-2026-2027/)\n- [Professional master’s fees (alternate schedule)](https://www.purdue.edu/treasurer/finance/bursar-office/tuition/fee-rates-2026-2027/professional-masters-program-fees-2026-2027/)\n- [Application Steps and Process (Fall 2027 / Spring 2027 dates)](https://cs.purdue.edu/graduate/admission/steps.html)\n- [Admission FAQ (Dec 1 / Oct 1 month-day)](https://www.cs.purdue.edu/graduate/admission/faq-application.html)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
