    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/texas-cs.md",
    "title": "UT Austin — MS",
    "body": "# UT Austin — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#10 in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Texas at Austin\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nOn-campus research MSCS: breadth (3) + minor (2), then coursework (5 electives) or thesis (3 electives + 2 thesis courses); typically ~10 courses / ~2 years. Distinct from the online MSCS.\n\nOrientation: Research MSCS · Coursework or thesis · ~2 years\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$18,162 — Academic-year tuition and fees (Natural Sciences nonresident graduate, 9 hours × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nGraduate Nonresident Natural Sciences: 9 semester hours = $9,081 per semester → $18,162 for Fall+Spring. At 12 hours: $10,970/semester. Separately, the catalog lists Option III Computer Science (MSCompSci) total program fee estimate $10,000 (same resident/nonresident)—commonly associated with the online/CDSO pathway. Confirm with UTCS which schedule applies to a specific on-campus research MS offer.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 15 Oct · Deadline 15 Dec (Fall only; month-day as posted — year not labeled on UTCS apply page). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s: no automatic funding. Teaching/research positions may be available; summer FoCS internships mentioned. PhD funding must not be applied to MS.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [PhD and MS research degrees](https://www.cs.utexas.edu/graduate/research-degrees)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://catalog.utexas.edu/general-information/registration-tuition-and-fees/tuition-and-fees/tables-tuition-for-fall-and-spring/)\n- [Tuition rates hub](https://onestop.utexas.edu/managing-costs/cost-tuition-rates/tuition-rates/)\n- [Cost & aid](https://www.cs.utexas.edu/graduate/cost-and-aid)\n- [UT tuition tables PDF (catalog)](https://catalog.utexas.edu/general-information/registration-tuition-and-fees/tuition-and-fees/tables-tuition-for-fall-and-spring/tables-tuition-for-fall-and-spring.pdf)\n- [UTCS graduate apply / important dates](https://www.cs.utexas.edu/graduate/apply)\n- [UT Graduate degrees & programs (CS Fall only; Dec. 15)](https://graduate.utexas.edu/degrees-programs)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
