    "title": "UCLA — MS",
    "body": "# UCLA — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, Los Angeles\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCLA CS MS: nine 4-unit courses (B- or better) plus three CS 201 seminars. Thesis (CS 598) or Capstone project plans; no fixed core list — majority CS coursework.\n\nOrientation: 36 units · Thesis or capstone · Flexible coursework\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$38,233 — Academic-year tuition and mandatory fees (Academic Master, nonresident, continuing); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUCLA Registrar public fee tables Academic Master annual 2026–27 nonresident continuing total $38,232.76 (Tuition $13,722 + NRST $15,102 + Student Services Fee $1,344 + UCSHIP $7,516.98 + campus fees). California resident continuing total without NRST $23,130.76. Grad Division rounds these to about $38,233 / $23,131. New students add one-time Document Fee $97.43. CS MS uses the standard Academic Master schedule (not a self-supporting program). NRST PhD candidacy waiver does not apply to MS.\n\nApplication timing: Apps mid-Sep · Deadline 15 Dec 2026 · 23:59 Pacific (MS/PhD Fall only — Grad Division 2027–28). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nThe department explicitly does not guarantee TA, graduate student researcher or reader positions to MS students.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CS Graduate Admissions](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-admissions/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Registrar public fees)](https://sa.ucla.edu/RO/Fees/Public/public-fees)\n- [Grad Division tuition summary](https://grad.ucla.edu/funding/tuition/)\n- [Financial aid COA](https://financialaid.ucla.edu/graduate-aid/cost-of-attendance)\n- [CS Graduate Application Requirements (Dec 15 23:59 PT; mid-Sep open)](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-requirements/)\n- [UCLA Grad Division CS 2027–2028 requirements (deadline Dec 15, 2026)](https://grad.ucla.edu/gasaa/deptinfo/deptinfo.asp?academicyear=20272028&code=0201)\n- [CS Grad Admissions FAQ](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-admission-frequently-asked-questions/)\n- [Program requirements (Grad Division)](https://grad.ucla.edu/graduate-program-requirements/program-requirements-for-computer-science-7-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2/)\n- [Graduate student handbook](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-student-handbook/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
