    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/usc-cs.md",
    "title": "USC — MS",
    "body": "# USC — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#21 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Southern California\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUSC Viterbi MS CS (General): 32 units with CSCI 570 + electives; thesis and many specializations available; FT often 1.5–2 years.\n\nOrientation: 32 units · CSCI 570 · Specializations / thesis\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$43,872 — Academic-year tuition (Viterbi graduate engineering, 8 units × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUSC Viterbi Graduate Tuition Fall 2026–Summer 2027: $2,742 per unit (same for on-campus and DEN@Viterbi). MS Computer Science requires 32 units (thesis option adds 4). Typical full-time pace in Viterbi COA examples is 8 units/semester → AY tuition $2,742 × 8 × 2 = $43,872. Full 32-unit program tuition at the published rate = $87,744. Mandatory fees about $922/semester (health center, Topping, programming, transportation; first semester adds one-time $55 orientation) not included in the tuition figure. Health insurance separate.\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 final 15 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. PT · Scholarship consideration 15 Dec (Fall 2027 row; year not printed on that cell). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [USC CS Master's programs](https://www.cs.usc.edu/academic-programs/masters/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://viterbigradadmission.usc.edu/programs/masters/tuition-funding/tuition-funding-masters/)\n- [32-unit MS COA PDF](https://viterbigradadmission.usc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/2026-2027-Tuition-and-Fees-32.pdf)\n- [Viterbi MS CS](https://viterbigradadmission.usc.edu/programs/masters/msprograms/computer-science/ms-computer-science/)\n- [USC Viterbi Master's Application Deadlines](https://viterbigradadmission.usc.edu/programs/masters/apply/)\n- [MS CS General](https://www.cs.usc.edu/academic-programs/masters/computer-science-general/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
