    "body": "# Yale — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#21 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Yale University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nYale CS terminal MS: one-year (8 courses) or selective two-year (6 courses + thesis + teaching). Visa students on one-year track take 4 degree courses per term.\n\nOrientation: 1-year (8 courses) or 2-year thesis · Terminal MS\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$52,400 — Academic-year tuition (GSAS full-time master’s); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nYale Graduate School of Arts and Sciences Tuition and Fees 2026–27: full-time study $26,200 per term → $52,400 AY. Half-time $13,100/term; one-quarter time $6,550/term. Continuous Registration Fee $880/term; Yale Health Hospitalization/Specialty Coverage $3,764 for twelve months—fees not included in the tuition figure. CS one-year MS is typically eight courses (four per term for visa full-time); two-year research/TF track exists with limited places. Most one-year MS students pay tuition themselves.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open (Fall 2027 application available) · Deadline 2 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. ET (CS MS). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS program](https://engineering.yale.edu/academic-study/departments/computer-science/graduate-study/master-science-program)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://gsas.yale.edu/resources/graduate-financial-aid/tuition-and-fees)\n- [Student Accounts GSAS rates](https://student-accounts.yale.edu/tuition-and-fees)\n- [GSAS Dates & Deadlines (CS MS Jan 2, 2027; Fall 2027 reply Apr 15)](https://gsas.yale.edu/admissions/phdmasters-application-process/dates-deadlines)\n- [GSAS Computer Science](https://gsas.yale.edu/programs-of-study/computer-science)\n- [GSAS PhD/Master's application process (Fall 2027 app available)](https://gsas.yale.edu/admissions/phdmasters-application-process)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
