    "body": "# Georgia Terry — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#25 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Georgia\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUGA Terry Full-Time MBA: ~22 months, 61 credits with Y1 cores/analytics, Y2 legal + dual capstones + electives; summer internship.\n\nOrientation: ~22 months · 61 credits · Dual capstones\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$36,000 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA Athens, Non-Resident); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUGA Terry Full-Time MBA Tuition and Fees 2026–2027: Non-Resident Tuition $36,000; Georgia Resident $14,064; Out-of-Country $37,032. Student Fees $1,494 (all) — Total Tuition + Fees 1 Year Non-Resident $37,494 / Resident $15,558 / Out-of-Country $38,526. One-time nonrefundable MBA Program Fee $500 and PreMBA Coursework $170 separate. UGA Bursar Fall 2026/Spring 2027: MBA Athens Out-of-State 12+ hrs $18,000/semester (= $36,000 AY). Full-time Athens MBA only — not Online/Executive/Fast Track Professional MBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 10 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. ET (Full-Time MBA; R1 passed; recommended for internationals). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-053, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-Time MBA curriculum](https://www.terry.uga.edu/mba/fulltime/curriculum/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.terry.uga.edu/mba/fulltime/admissions/tuition/)\n- [UGA Bursar tuition & fees 2026–27](https://busfin.uga.edu/finance-division/bursar/students-parents/bursar-tuition-fees/2026-2027/)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions (deadlines)](https://www.terry.uga.edu/mba/fulltime/admissions/)\n- [Full-Time MBA program](https://www.terry.uga.edu/mba/fulltime/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
