    "title": "UT Dallas Jindal — MBA",
    "body": "# UT Dallas Jindal — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#23 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Texas at Dallas\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUT Dallas Full-Time MBA Cohort: ~18–21 months, 53 hours (32 core + 21 electives), lock-step with pre-fall boot camp.\n\nOrientation: ~18–21 months · 53 hours · Cohort\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$36,532 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA, Nonresident; Fall I + Spring I); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUT Dallas MBA Cost & Tuition Plan 2026–2027 Estimated Variable Tuition (Full-Time MBA): Nonresident Cost $18,266 Fall I + $18,266 Spring I = $36,532 academic year (matches Bursar Non-Resident/Graduate Variable 2026–27 rate at 12+ SCH). Resident Cost $9,111/semester ($18,222 AY). Separate MBA/program Fees column $1,500 Fall I + $1,700 Spring I = $3,200 AY (MGT supplemental $100/SCH) not included in the $36,532. Published full-program Nonresident Tuition on 53 credits $60,307 + Fees $5,300 = $65,607 — full-duration totals, not used as the annual figure. School states all Full-Time admits get ≥$1,000 merit scholarship qualifying for resident rates; nonresident sticker used per OOS-primary rule. Full-time MBA only — not Professional/Online.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 8 Jan (month-day; year not labeled on official FT MBA deadlines table; fall start; R1 Oct 15 passed if same annual cycle). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-057, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-Time MBA curriculum](https://mba.utdallas.edu/academics/full-time-mba/curriculum/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://mba.utdallas.edu/tuition-value/)\n- [Bursar tuition rates 2026–27](https://bursar.utdallas.edu/tuition/tuition-rates/)\n- [Full-Time MBA academics](https://mba.utdallas.edu/academics/full-time-mba/)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions (deadlines table)](https://mba.utdallas.edu/admissions/full-time-mba/)\n- [MBA programs hub](https://mba.utdallas.edu/)\n- [Catalog Business Administration](https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2026/graduate/programs/jsom/business-administration)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
