    "title": "Vanderbilt Owen — MBA",
    "body": "# Vanderbilt Owen — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#16 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Vanderbilt University\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nOwen Full-Time MBA: 2 years, ≥62 credits across eight modules; required cores, ethics, and at least one 12-credit concentration.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · ≥62 credits · Concentrations\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$76,700 — Academic-year tuition (Owen Full-Time MBA); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nVanderbilt Owen MBA Tuition & Financing and Student Accounts Graduate/Professional Tuition and Fees 2026–2027 both list Owen Graduate School of Management Tuition $76,700 per year. Separate first-year direct costs include Maintenance Fee $1,250, Transcript Fee $100 (first Fall), Student Services Fee $694, Student Health Fee $882; health insurance and living expenses are additional. Full-time MBA only — not Executive MBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 6 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. CT (Fall 2027; R1 passed; apps opened 19 Aug 2026). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nThe program describes individualized career support and preparation before internships. Placement difficulty and international-specific results have not been evaluated.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-051, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MBA program](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/mba/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/mba/admissions/tuition-financing-scholarships/)\n- [Student Accounts 2026–27 grad/prof fees](https://www.vanderbilt.edu/stuaccts/fees/tuition_fees_2026-27_grad_prof/)\n- [MBA Admissions (Fall 2027 deadlines)](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/mba/admissions/)\n- [MBA Application Instructions (11:59 p.m. CT)](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/mba/admissions/application-instructions/)\n- [Applications for Fall 2027 Open August 19](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/news/2026/08/14/vanderbilt-business-applications-fall-2027-open-august-19/)\n- [MBA curriculum](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/mba/curriculum/)\n- [Owen catalog 2025-26 PDF](https://registrar.vanderbilt.edu/documents/Owen-Graduate-School-of-Management-Catalog-2025-26.pdf)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
