    "title": "Yale SOM — MBA",
    "body": "# Yale SOM — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Yale University\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nYale SOM MBA: 2 years, 72 units. Integrated Year-1 core (Orientation + Organizational Perspectives) then Year-2 electives; summer internship required.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 72 units · Integrated core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$90,900 — Academic-year tuition (Yale SOM MBA); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nYale SOM Affording Your MBA Cost Information lists Cost of Attendance 2026–27 with Tuition $90,900 and Program Fee $500 (Total Tuition and Fees $91,400). Living expenses, books, transportation, and Yale Health insurance ($3,764) are separate; total single-student budget $128,976. Joint-degree fees may differ.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 6 Jan 2027 (Fall 2027 / 2026–27 cycle; R1 passed; clock time not on table). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nAll full-time MBA students complete Scholarship Application after admission for Yale SOM scholarships; international students eligible for school scholarships (country-specific awards also exist). Median award figure is Class of 2027 statistic, not a guarantee.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-005, SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-082, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Integrated curriculum](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/curriculum)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/affording-your-mba/cost-information)\n- [Affording Your MBA](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/affording-your-mba)\n- [MBA Application Information (deadlines)](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information)\n- [MBA Admissions](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions)\n- [MBA program](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba)\n- [MBA curriculum (catalog)](https://catalog.yale.edu/management/full-time-mba/mba-curriculum/)\n- [Core courses](https://catalog.yale.edu/management/courses/mba-core-courses/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
