    "title": "Arizona Eller — MSF",
    "body": "# Arizona Eller — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#30 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE programs remain on a separate track.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Arizona\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nArizona Eller MSF: STEM, 30 cr, ~9 mo Tucson. Deadlines Oct 15 early / May 15 intl / Jun 1 FINPREP / Aug 1 final (years for F27). Tuition NR $47,500 / AZ $27,200 (2026–27).\n\nOrientation: Fall · ~9 months · STEM · TFE #30 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$47,500 — Non-resident tuition — Tucson on-campus MS Finance 9-month / 30 units (Eller Matrix 2026–27); 2026–27 (Eller graduate programs matrix PDF dated Aug 2026).\n\nSTEM; ~9 months Tucson on-campus; 30 units. Open external/intl. Prefer matrix sticker ($47,500 NR / $27,200 AZ) as official 2026–27 program matrix; ROI page itemization differs by ~$78. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: Arizona resident tuition — 9-month Tucson MSF (2026–27 matrix) $27,200. Matrix footnote: tuition and fees subject to change. ROI page itemizes AZ resident 9-mo total $27,122 and Non-AZ $47,422 (slightly below matrix round numbers) including program fees/fees lines; $500 seat fee due after admission applied toward tuition if student attends. FINPrep non-credit summer module $2,500 separate if required. Online MSF listed separately $37,500 ($1,250/unit) — different modality. STEM; ~9 months Tucson on-campus; 30 units. Open external/intl. Prefer matrix sticker ($47,500 NR / $27,200 AZ) as official 2026–27 program matrix; ROI page itemization differs by ~$78.\n\nApplication timing: Fall Early Admission · 2026-10-15 · Bullet list used; same page also mentions Dec 1 preferred intl / Feb 1 — confirm. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-125.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-125. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance)\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/admissions)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://eller.arizona.edu/sites/default/files/2026-08/Matrix-2026-2027.pdf)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Eller MSF Cost / ROI](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/roi)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
