    "body": "# Illinois Gies — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#19 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE programs remain on a separate track.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nIllinois Gies MSF: STEM, ~3 semesters / 40 cr. Fall 2027 rounds Oct 28’26–Jun 9’27 (intl final May 5). Est. intl tuition+fees $76,443 / resident $57,846 (2026–27 3-sem).\n\nOrientation: Fall or Spring · ~15 months / 40 cr · STEM · TFE #19 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$67,800 — Gies MSF international tuition total — 3 semesters × $22,600 (2026–27 estimates); 2026–27 estimates (table shows Fall '26 / Spring '27 / Fall '27 sequence for Fall 2026 cohort). Fall 2027 entrants: analogous 3-semester sequence; later-term rates may change — tuition guarantee locks entering-cohort rate once enrolled..\n\nMSF assessed per semester (not per credit), up to 20 credits/semester. US resident 3-semester total tuition+fees $57,846 (tuition $49,437 + fees $8,409). International total tuition+fees $76,443. Open external admits (not a UF/TAMU-style combination). Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: US resident tuition+campus fees estimate — 3 semesters (2026–27 rates) $57,846. Mandatory fees reference: $8,643. Campus fees international $2,881 × 3 semesters = $8,643 (2026–27 estimates on Gies MSF tuition page). Non-refundable deposit $1,750 credited to tuition after 10th day of first semester. MSF assessed per semester (not per credit), up to 20 credits/semester. US resident 3-semester total tuition+fees $57,846 (tuition $49,437 + fees $8,409). International total tuition+fees $76,443. Open external admits (not a UF/TAMU-style combination). Living cost band from official COA: $21,402–$29,705 (Registrar 2026–27 Grad additional expenses (intl): Food & Housing $16,512 + Books & Supplies $1,800 + Other $3,090 = $21,402 per academic year. Gies MSF domestic COA PDF lists Additional Expenses $9,935/semester (Food & Housing $7,490 + Books $900 + Other $1,545) → ×3 semesters = $29,705 (lifestyle-dependent).).\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 — Round 1 · 2026-10-28. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-110.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-110. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf)\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/admissions)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/tuition)\n- [Curriculum / credits](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/curriculum)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Gies MSF Estimated COA PDF (domestic 26–27)](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/docs/default-source/default-document-library/estimated-cost-of-attendance---gies-msf-domestic-26-27-(1).pdf?sfvrsn=787204dc_2)\n- [Illinois Registrar 26/27 Grad Additional Expenses](https://www.registrar.illinois.edu/tuition-fees/tuition-fee-rates/tf-rates-academic-year/g-additional-expenses-2627/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
