    "title": "Princeton BCF — MSF",
    "body": "# Princeton BCF — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#2 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE programs remain on a separate track.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Princeton University\n\nDegree route: Master in Finance (M.Fin.)\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nPrinceton M.Fin.: Fall 2027 apps open; deadline Dec 15, 2026 11:59pm ET. Four-semester curriculum + summer internship. AY 2026–27 tuition $65,210 (+ SHP $4,220).\n\nOrientation: Fall start · ~2 years · TFE #2 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$65,210 — Academic-year regular graduate tuition (per year, 2026–27); 2026–27.\n\nM.Fin. typically 4 semesters / 2 academic years (compressed 2-semester option for select admits after admission). Two-year tuition ≈ 2×$65,210 before SHP; SHP charged each year of enrollment. Missing ≠ full-degree total. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nStudent Health Plan (SHP) fee $4,220 AY; tuition+SHP total $69,430 per year (Graduate School rates). M.Fin. typically 4 semesters / 2 academic years (compressed 2-semester option for select admits after admission). Two-year tuition ≈ 2×$65,210 before SHP; SHP charged each year of enrollment. Missing ≠ full-degree total. University regular tuition rate; M.Fin. is typically 2 academic years (4 semesters). Living costs separate. Living cost band from official COA: $33,141–$39,770 (Princeton Graduate School published living expenses 2026–27: $33,141 (10 months) / $39,770 (12 months) — housing, food, personal, books & supplies.).\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 application deadline · 2026-12-15 · 11:59 p.m. Eastern. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-086. MBA-only merit cards (e.g. SCH-025, SCH-052, SCH-056) are not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-086. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Fall 2027 apps open](https://bcf.princeton.edu/news/apply-for-the-fall-2027-master-in-finance-program/)\n- [Graduate School Finance field](https://gradschool.princeton.edu/academics/degrees-requirements/fields-study/finance)\n- [Apply page](https://bcf.princeton.edu/academic-programs/master-in-finance/apply-for-the-master-in-finance-program/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://gradschool.princeton.edu/financial-support/financial-support-model/funding-calendar-university-rates-costs)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
