    "body": "# UT Dallas Jindal — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#16 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE programs remain on a separate track.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: The University of Texas at Dallas\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUTD Jindal MS Finance: STEM, 36 credits. Flex deadlines May 1 fall / Oct 1 spring / Mar 1 summer. Cohort ~12 mo: OOS $50k / in-state $35k; foreign deadline Apr 30. Flex COA via UTD tuition plans.\n\nOrientation: Fall/Spring/Summer Flex or summer Cohort · 36 cr · STEM · TFE #16 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$50,000 — MS Finance Cohort out-of-state / non-Texas total tuition and fees for the degree; 2026–27 · as published on MS Finance Cohort page (Fall 2027 cycle; subject to change).\n\nCFA-aligned cohort; ~12-month, 36 semester credit hours. Summer start of sequence (Semester 1 summer courses). High-achieving admits auto-considered for scholarship levels applied to tuition; awards do NOT create in-state tuition status. Cohort students excluded from general JSOM graduate scholarship portal — contact program director. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nPublished $50,000 (OOS) / $35,000 (TX resident) are total tuition and fees for the degree (includes program activities, internship/capstone, communication training, career coaching, business school per-credit fee). Living and health insurance extra. Paid in two installments (fall and spring). CFA-aligned cohort; ~12-month, 36 semester credit hours. Summer start of sequence (Semester 1 summer courses). High-achieving admits auto-considered for scholarship levels applied to tuition; awards do NOT create in-state tuition status. Cohort students excluded from general JSOM graduate scholarship portal — contact program director. SUMMER START — matriculation is not a standard autumn-only Fall intake.\n\nApplication timing: Flex — Fall regular · 2027-05-01. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-104. MBA-only merit (SCH-057) is not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-104. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [2026 Graduate Catalog — Finance](https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2026/graduate/programs/jsom/finance)\n- [MS Finance FAQ](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-faq/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://fin.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-cohort/)\n- [MS degree options](https://fin.utdallas.edu/masters-degree-options/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [JSOM Graduate Scholarships (cohort exclusion note)](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/student-resources/scholarships/graduate-scholarships/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
