    "path": "04-scholarships/opportunities/gsu-msf-graduate-assistantships.md",
    "title": "Georgia State Robinson MS Finance Graduate Assistantships (SCH-088)",
    "body": "# Georgia State Robinson MS Finance Graduate Assistantships (SCH-088)\n\n- **Category:** Assistantship · **Type:** assistantship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** Auto-considered at admission; also post-admit Handshake applications\n- **Scope:** gsu-msf\n- **Programs:** gsu-msf\n- **HK eligible:** yes · **TW eligible:** yes · **International:** yes · **PRC:** yes\n\n## Summary\nGraduate research/administrative assistantships offset MS Finance costs. Applicants with completed applications are automatically considered for GA awards at admission; others may apply via Handshake after deposit. For Finance (12-month) sample: GA tuition waiver $14,865.50 + stipend estimate $5,000; out-of-country remaining cost with stipend ≈ $29,513.50 (published sample; subject to change). F-1 students are eligible. Cannot be counted toward I-20 minimum funding.\n\n## Eligibility\nAdmitted RCB graduate students; min 3.0 GPA; register 9 credits fall/spring (6 summer); U.S. work authorization — F-1 eligible (need SSN after hire). Priority GA consideration: apply by Round 2 (Jan 25, 2027) for Fall 2027. Intl needing visa must apply by Round 3 (Mar 15, 2027).\n\n## Amount\nSample Finance 12-mo: waiver $14,865.50 + stipend ~$5,000 (published breakdown; varies by appointment)\n\n## Deadline\nPriority with Round 2 app (2027-01-25); positions also post near term start\n\n## Notes\nEvening Buckhead MSF — GA requires weekday daytime campus availability (8:30 a.m.–5:00 p.m.), which may conflict with work schedules.\n\n## Sources\n- [Robinson Graduate Assistantships](https://robinson.gsu.edu/graduate-student-resources/graduate-assistantships/)\n- [Finance MS program costs](https://www.gsu.edu/program/finance-ms/)\n- [International applicants — GA not for I-20](https://robinson.gsu.edu/admissions/international-applicants/)\n\n_Do not treat amounts/deadlines as final; re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
