    "body": "# RIT Graduate Tuition Scholarships (Finance MS) (SCH-123)\n\n- **Category:** Merit-Based · **Type:** scholarship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** Automatic with admission\n- **Scope:** rit-msf\n- **Programs:** rit-msf\n- **HK eligible:** yes · **TW eligible:** yes · **International:** yes · **PRC:** yes\n\n## Summary\nConsidered for RIT graduate scholarships just by applying; no separate application. Typically 10–40% tuition scholarship range; amount varies by student and department. Offered to top candidates for academic excellence. Scholarship letter in admissions portal at acceptance. Not stackable with other RIT scholarships. Online tuition-rate programs excluded. International applicants not living in the U.S. may qualify for these (distinct from Master Up residency rule).\n\n## Eligibility\nAdmitted on-campus Finance MS students (qualifying graduate programs). Scholarships cannot be combined with Master Up / Master Plan / Combined Accelerated.\n\n## Amount\nTypically 10–40% of tuition\n\n## Deadline\nWith admission (rolling)\n\n## Notes\nMaster Up (30%) is separate restricted card SCH-124.\n\n## Sources\n- [RIT Graduate Funding Sources](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/financial-aid/graduate-funding-sources)\n- [Estimate Graduate Education Costs](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/graduate/estimate-education-costs)\n- [Finance MS](https://www.rit.edu/study/finance-ms)\n\n_Do not treat amounts/deadlines as final; re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
